  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">TZ SEED TRUST - Employment opportunities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The grant applied to SEED TRUST intends to build YWDs&apos; capacity for vocational and business skills in achieving equal rights and employment opportunities. Moreover, it will promote the engagement of stakeholders in offering employment opportunities. It will also promote the creation of enabling environment for YWDs to access funding opportunities from the local government.
The project main objective is to enhance 60 youth with disabilities between 18-30 years old in Morogoro Municipality council access to equal rights andemployment opportunities by February 2024.
Among the activities that will be implemented include:
1. Identify and assess vulnerability of target YWDs
2. Conduct five-day entrepreneurship training on business development to 60 YWDs
3. Support 10 YWDs   participatein vocational training
4. Reward innovative best 10 YWDs with seed money for IGAs
5. Provide mentorship support to trainees to develop business skills capacities
6. Link trained YWDs to local business/entrepreneurs for apprenticeship.
7. Conduct a one- day quarterly advocacy meeting with 30 stakeholders to influence creation of enabling environment for YWDs to access employment opportunities
8. Link YWDs to stakeholder&#x2019;s forums for accessing funding, marketing and networking opportunities.
9. Conduct a three-day training 20 YWDs on lobbying and advocacy skills
10. Facilitate YWDs advocate&#x2019;s quarterly advocacy meetings for reinforcement of PWDs Act Number 9 of 2010, Section 31.
11. Develop and host SEED Trust Website and social Media Network account for advocacy and marketing of YWDs activities.
12. Hold one-day advocacy meeting with local government officials to create enabling environment for YWDs to access loans from District youth development funds.</narrative>
  </description>
